  "sortOrder": 54004,
  "verseCount": 16,
  "aliases": [
    "1 Tim",
    "1Tim",
    "1 Ti",
    "1Ti"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Now the Spirit speaketh expressly, that in the latter times some shall depart from the faith, giving heed to seducing spirits, and doctrines of devils;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Speaking lies in hypocrisy; having their conscience seared with a hot iron;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Forbidding to marry, and commanding to abstain from meats, which God hath created to be received with thanksgiving of them which believe and know the truth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For every creature of God is good, and nothing to be refused, if it be received with thanksgiving:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For it is sanctified by the word of God and prayer.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "If thou put the brethren in remembrance of these things, thou shalt be a good minister of Jesus Christ, nourished up in the words of faith and of good doctrine, whereunto thou hast attained.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "But refuse profane and old wives’ fables, and exercise thyself rather unto godliness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "For bodily exercise profiteth little: but godliness is profitable unto all things, having promise of the life that now is, and of that which is to come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "This is a faithful saying and worthy of all acceptation.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "For therefore we both labour and suffer reproach, because we trust in the living God, who is the Saviour of all men, specially of those that believe.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "These things command and teach.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Let no man despise thy youth; but be thou an example of the believers, in word, in conversation, in charity, in spirit, in faith, in purity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Till I come, give attendance to reading, to exhortation, to doctrine.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Neglect not the gift that is in thee, which was given thee by prophecy, with the laying on of the hands of the presbytery.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Meditate upon these things; give thyself wholly to them; that thy profiting may appear to all.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-timothy:4:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Take heed unto thyself, and unto the doctrine; continue in them: for in doing this thou shalt both save thyself, and them that hear thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Timothy 4:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-timothy:4:16"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
